1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,399
Laddoo Lab now sells in ten local
shops, a supermarket chain and an online

2
00:00:05,399 --> 00:00:06,299
shop.

3
00:00:06,289 --> 00:00:10,406
But during the festive offer, the
supermarket shelf sat empty for a whole

4
00:00:10,406 --> 00:00:11,306
week.

5
00:00:11,459 --> 00:00:14,373
Nobody noticed, until
the store manager called.

6
00:00:14,373 --> 00:00:17,157
There was no plan, and
nobody was checking.

7
00:00:17,807 --> 00:00:20,871
So Zoya calls the team
to Nani's kitchen table.

8
00:00:21,221 --> 00:00:23,411
Arjun brings the sales numbers.

9
00:00:23,411 --> 00:00:25,497
Dev brings the online orders.

10
00:00:25,497 --> 00:00:28,125
Nani knows what the kitchen can make.

11
00:00:28,474 --> 00:00:32,419
Together, they will write next year's
marketing plan, and check it every

12
00:00:32,419 --> 00:00:33,319
month.

13
00:00:33,601 --> 00:00:36,146
So what are marketing
planning and control?

14
00:00:36,446 --> 00:00:38,672
A marketing plan is a written map.

15
00:00:39,022 --> 00:00:42,941
It says where you are now, where you
want to go, and how you will get there.

16
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:47,369
Marketing control means checking
the real results against the plan.

17
00:00:47,719 --> 00:00:51,324
When something goes off track,
you find out why, and you fix it.

18
00:00:51,974 --> 00:00:54,924
A good marketing plan
answers four questions.

19
00:00:55,274 --> 00:00:56,174
One.

20
00:00:55,761 --> 00:00:57,041
Where are we now?

21
00:00:57,041 --> 00:01:01,309
The shops and the supermarket are
strong, but online sales are weak.

22
00:01:01,659 --> 00:01:02,559
Two.

23
00:01:02,128 --> 00:01:03,749
Where do we want to go?

24
00:01:03,749 --> 00:01:06,363
A clear goal, with a number and a date.

25
00:01:06,363 --> 00:01:09,576
Three thousand four hundred
packs a month, by March.

26
00:01:09,926 --> 00:01:10,826
Three.

27
00:01:10,423 --> 00:01:11,768
How will we get there?

28
00:01:11,768 --> 00:01:14,580
Who does what, by when,
and with how much money.

29
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:15,830
Four.

30
00:01:15,472 --> 00:01:16,817
How will we check?

31
00:01:16,817 --> 00:01:19,903
Count the packs sold
every week, shop by shop.

32
00:01:20,553 --> 00:01:23,392
Now watch control at work, in four steps.

33
00:01:23,742 --> 00:01:24,642
Step one.

34
00:01:24,613 --> 00:01:25,760
Set the goal.

35
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,979
The plan says three
thousand packs in January.

36
00:01:29,329 --> 00:01:30,229
Step two.

37
00:01:30,209 --> 00:01:31,109
Measure.

38
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:33,170
Arjun counts sales every week.

39
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,087
January ends at three thousand and fifty.

40
00:01:36,087 --> 00:01:36,987
On track.

41
00:01:37,317 --> 00:01:40,577
In February, the goal is
three thousand two hundred.

42
00:01:40,577 --> 00:01:43,023
Only two thousand six hundred are sold.

43
00:01:43,373 --> 00:01:44,319
Step three.

44
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:45,533
Find the cause.

45
00:01:45,533 --> 00:01:48,124
Dev checks each week, shop by shop.

46
00:01:48,474 --> 00:01:51,699
In week three, the
supermarket shelf was empty.

47
00:01:51,699 --> 00:01:54,357
Arjun refilled it only every two weeks.

48
00:01:54,707 --> 00:01:55,607
Step four.

49
00:01:55,587 --> 00:01:56,487
Fix it.

50
00:01:56,316 --> 00:01:58,694
Experts call this corrective action.

51
00:01:58,694 --> 00:02:01,345
Arjun now refills the shelf every week.

52
00:02:01,695 --> 00:02:05,269
In March, sales reach three
thousand four hundred and fifty.

53
00:02:05,269 --> 00:02:07,875
Back on track, and the loop starts again.

54
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:10,089
A plan shows the road.

55
00:02:10,089 --> 00:02:11,748
Control keeps you on it.

56
00:02:12,448 --> 00:02:15,886
Kotler and Keller name four
kinds of marketing control.

57
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,624
Annual plan control.

58
00:02:17,624 --> 00:02:19,371
Are we hitting our goals?

59
00:02:19,371 --> 00:02:23,554
A phone maker checks sales against
its yearly target, every month.

60
00:02:23,904 --> 00:02:25,379
Profitability control.

61
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:27,496
Where do we really make money?

62
00:02:27,496 --> 00:02:31,108
A bakery finds which items
earn, and which ones lose.

63
00:02:31,458 --> 00:02:32,903
Efficiency control.

64
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:34,698
Is every rupee working?

65
00:02:34,698 --> 00:02:38,868
A food delivery app checks how
many orders each ad brings.

66
00:02:39,218 --> 00:02:40,487
Strategic control.

67
00:02:40,487 --> 00:02:42,707
Are we still on the right road?

68
00:02:42,707 --> 00:02:47,137
A bank asks if its branches still
suit customers who now use phones.

69
00:02:47,787 --> 00:02:49,449
But can planning go wrong?

70
00:02:49,449 --> 00:02:51,488
Yes, if you hold on too tight.

71
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:52,940
The good side.

72
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:56,390
Everyone knows their job,
and problems show up early.

73
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:57,863
The hard side.

74
00:02:57,863 --> 00:03:02,504
Plans can turn into paperwork, and
numbers can miss what customers feel.

75
00:03:02,854 --> 00:03:07,623
In April, Arjun wants Nani to double
the batch, fast, to hit four thousand

76
00:03:07,623 --> 00:03:08,523
packs.

77
00:03:08,568 --> 00:03:09,704
Nani says no.

78
00:03:09,704 --> 00:03:11,482
No shortcuts with taste.

79
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:14,513
So Zoya changes the goal, not the recipe.

80
00:03:14,863 --> 00:03:18,125
President Dwight
Eisenhower said it in 1957.

81
00:03:18,125 --> 00:03:21,729
Plans are worthless, but
planning is everything.

82
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:22,979
The lesson?

83
00:03:22,917 --> 00:03:26,286
Check often, and change the
plan when the facts change.

84
00:03:26,936 --> 00:03:27,981
Quick check.

85
00:03:27,981 --> 00:03:29,910
February sales fall short.

86
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,950
Zoya finds out why, and Arjun
changes his delivery days.

87
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,113
What is this?

88
00:03:37,013 --> 00:03:38,169
Marketing control!

89
00:03:38,169 --> 00:03:41,753
They measured, found the cause,
and took corrective action.

90
00:03:42,353 --> 00:03:43,366
So, remember.

91
00:03:43,666 --> 00:03:47,546
A marketing plan says where you are,
where you are going, and how you will

92
00:03:47,546 --> 00:03:48,446
get there.

93
00:03:48,592 --> 00:03:52,570
Control means: set the goal,
measure, find the cause, and fix it.

94
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,744
Check often, and stay
ready to change the plan.

95
00:03:56,344 --> 00:03:59,781
Next time, we'll explore
customer relationship management.
